@hugeicons-pro:registry=https://npm.hugeicons.com/

# The auth token for the registry above deliberately does NOT live here. pnpm
# refuses to expand environment variables in registry credentials read from a
# committed .npmrc, so a `${HUGEICONS_PRO_TOKEN}` line here is silently ignored
# and every install 401s on @hugeicons-pro/*.
#
# Locally, put it in your user-level config:
#
#   vp pm config set --global "//npm.hugeicons.com/:_authToken" "<token>"
#
# On EAS it arrives as the `NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG` file variable, which holds a
# whole .npmrc and whose env value is the path EAS materialises it at. That is
# read as user config, so the credential is trusted. It cannot be done from an
# `eas-build-pre-install` hook: pnpm reinstalls the workspace before it runs any
# script, so the hook would execute only after the install it exists to fix.
